KG42.register("clusters-181bb49f91bdfbc5ef603427",{"id":"17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v142-d-K002","paper":"17-exogenous_cost_allocation","label":"Conditional allocation, partner incentives, and settlement of exogenous network charges","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"Conditional allocation, partner incentives, and settlement of exogenous network charges","market_meaning":"The system operator selects the applicable charge policy and provides network charges ex ante; participants make choices under different transaction costs within the permitted partner scope. Given the final negotiated quantities and prices for the same time period, the settlement chain calculates participants' signed receipts and payments and the operator's charge collection. The uniform charge, electrical-distance charge, and uniform zonal charge are retained as conditional branches respectively; partner inducement, contingency charge adjustment, and periodic revision are conditional policy uses and do not guarantee transaction execution, physical feasibility, or full cost recovery.","mechanism_ids":["v141-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["matching","settlement","coordination","clearing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Only charges for the same mechanism, applicable policy, transaction pair, and market time period are connected. The general differentiated zonal discussion in R005 and the uniform zonal example in R008 are retained separately; distance types and zone divisions cannot be tacitly interchanged. R003 shares only the exogenous-cost objective and charge composition, and the endogenous reference does not apply the charge schedule. R004 shares the ex ante publication, cross-period revision, and final quantity-price interfaces, and cross-period rate modification is not merged with iterative price updating into the same action.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The same network charge both enters transaction selection and forms a settlement deduction; on this basis, the source connects charge policy, partner incentives, dispatch objectives, and operator receipts. The partner-set constraint provides the tradable scope, but rate incentives are not equivalent to modifying that set. The negotiation solution remains primarily attributed to another cluster, and this cluster does not count its algorithmic obligations again.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries the meanings of partner permission, charge inducement, and conditional contingency response; dynamically modifying the partner set remains a discussed possibility."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the charge coefficients for each applicable policy, participants' receipts and payments, and the operator's charge collection, and is the result interface for cost allocation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides ex ante publication and cross-period adjustment of network charges and supplies the negotiated quantity-price interface to settlement; solution and stopping checks remain primarily attributed to the negotiation cluster."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Shares only the charge terms in the exogenous objective and the total-cost definition, explaining how charges enter decisions; it does not introduce the network-constraint guarantee of the endogenous reference."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::theta_gamma_nm","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-gamma-nm","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e21","v141-b-g01-e26","v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"The charge policy gives the applicable form of the charge coefficients, and the coordination chain provides the ex ante publication and conditional revision interface; they are combined only when the policy, time period, and transaction-direction conventions agree, and the three rates are not added together."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_d_nm"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E06"],"rationale":"The same distance-based charge policy explicitly incorporates distance into the charge and intends to encourage transactions with closer partners; this is a policy-incentive meaning, not a hard matching constraint guaranteeing selection of the nearest partner."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g02-E13"],"rationale":"The two chains respectively cover the uniform zonal charge example and the general differentiated zonal incentive, and belong to different conditional scopes of the same policy family; the uniform-charge formula cannot directly prove the differentiated effect in a specific high-price zone."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::theta_gamma_nm","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_gamma_n0"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T002","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-e21","v141-b-g01-e24"],"rationale":"The marginal and fixed terms of the same applicable charge are simultaneously used in the exogenous dispatch objective and in the settlement deduction; correspondence requires the same policy and time period, and the fixed term does not become a marginal incentive merely by entering the objective."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e25"],"rationale":"The separable charges in the objective connect to the charge collection reserved for the operator by each agent. Total cost, agents' net receipts and payments, and total collections are at different levels; these complete expressions cannot be judged as duplicate constraints, nor can full revenue adequacy be concluded on that basis."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-lambda-nm","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-p-nm"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_lambda_nm","v141-c-R008::x::x_p_nm","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e20","v141-b-g01-e24"],"rationale":"The final negotiated price and transaction quantity of the same transaction provide inputs to the payment relationship; any intermediate iteration does not automatically become a settlement result, and the stopping and reciprocity gaps remain associated with this interface."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_p_nm","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e15","v141-b-g01-e24"],"rationale":"The partner permission scope limits transaction pairs that may have nonzero transactions and payment aggregation; permission does not mandate execution, exit must be permitted by the power bounds, and charge policy also does not automatically rewrite the partner set."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-OM001","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T002","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-gamma-nm","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_gamma_nm"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e21","v141-b-g01-e24"],"rationale":"The generic network-charge parameter under the same policy, time period, and transaction direction is used in the objective, publication, and deduction respectively; the roles remain independent, and policy-specific coefficients of different policies are not unconditionally equated."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-OM002","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T003","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_gamma_n0"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e24"],"rationale":"The fixed charge of the same agent in the same time period enters the objective and the payment; not affecting the optimal quantity does not mean it can be deleted from settlement."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-OM003","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-lambda-nm","v141-c-R008::x::x_lambda_nm"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e24"],"rationale":"Only the final negotiated value of the corresponding transaction is bound as the settlement price input; the roles of iteration variable and final input are retained, and it is not claimed that all iteration prices are the same."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-OM004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-p-nm","v141-c-R008::x::x_p_nm"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e24"],"rationale":"The negotiated quantity and payment quantity correspond only under the same ordered transaction pair, time period, and final-result binding; both iterative proposals and settlement inputs are retained, and they are not interpreted as verified physical delivery."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"The evidence on charges, partner incentives, and settlement all remains unverified. Experimental eligibility permits this candidate assembly, but transcription, policy inferences, or the scientific correctness of settlement have not been verified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e25","v141-b-g01-e26","v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Humans check the evidence for each charge branch and interface, maintaining the original source_status; this assembly or assembled status must not be interpreted as independent source review or scientific approval."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G002","category":"scope_conflict","description":"Network charges are given ex ante, whereas each charge scheme in R008 selects the charge sign according to transaction direction. The source simultaneously permits prosumers to trade bidirectionally; if direction can change during negotiation, how the fixed coefficients and the post-transaction sign condition jointly hold has not yet been closed by a frozen rule.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e26","v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E13"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should verify whether transaction direction is fixed ex ante, or supplement source-supported conditions for handling bidirectional charging; D must not add absolute-value objectives or direction variables on its own or change the frozen linear charge terms."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G003","category":"scope_conflict","description":"R005-C002 discusses different zonal rates and high-price-zone incentives, whereas R008-C006 gives only an example of a uniform zonal unit charge. The complete charging rule for general differentiated zonal rates has no corresponding frozen object and cannot be replaced by the uniform example.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_u_zone","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_Nzone_nm"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g02-E13"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Retain the general zonal discussion and the uniform-rate special case separately; if calculation of differentiated zonal charges is required, upstream should supplement their conditions and expression from the source."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G004","category":"upstream_missing","description":"Distance and the number of cross-zone crossings are currently connected only as given parameters, and the selection of the electrical-distance method, the path, and the zone-counting procedure have not yet formed a frozen chain. How historical revenue and congestion information calibrate the unit charge is also only qualitatively described, and it cannot be claimed on that basis that a closed-loop cost-recovery control has been formed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_d_nm","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_Nzone_nm","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g02-E14"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If charge parameters need to be generated from the network topology, upstream must retain the distance method, zonal path, and their applicability conditions; parts of rate calibration without an explicitly source-stated algorithm continue to be marked as undetermined, and no numerical values are fabricated."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G005","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R008 labels transaction power in MW and transaction price in €/MWh, whereas the payment relationship is expressed per market time unit, with no time-period-length object provided. The monetary interpretation of the direct product must be consistent with the time unit, and it cannot be assumed by default to apply to any duration.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_p_nm","v141-c-R008::x::x_lambda_nm","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_u_uniq"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e26"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the conventions for power, transaction quantity, and monetary amount and rate per market time unit; if generalizing to non-hourly periods, upstream should provide source-supported unit handling, and no duration factor is added in D."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G006","category":"upstream_missing","description":"Participants' receipts and payments, their allocated network charges, and the operator's total collections exist only in the R008 expression and have no independent quantity objects that D can directly reference. Therefore, from total cost to collections, only an expression-level functional interface can currently be established, and no same-quantity mapping may be fabricated.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e25"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If magnitude-level tracking is required, upstream should complete the output quantities and bindings defined by the existing expression; D retains the level distinction among cost aggregation, net receipts and payments, and operator collections."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G007","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Existing nodes cover generic price signals, partner matching, and payments respectively, but do not explicitly represent the charge policy selected by the operator or the ex ante network charge. The related proposals all remain pending and cannot be regarded as approved nodes.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R005::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R008::V::settlement.payment"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e21","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e26","v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E13"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-network-charge","proposal:v141-b-g01-cost-allocation-policy","v141-b-g02-P01-network-charge","v141-b-g03-p01","v141-b-g03-p02"],"required_work":"Humans review the overlap and applicability scope of these proposals, and then decide whether upstream should extend; this time only existing objects are used to express the interface, and no policy, network-charge, or operator nodes are created."}]},"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R005","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R008","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R004","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-166b347ab5fcd2a9","COMP-486b93e7e3eb4336","COMP-739917e3869e45a6","COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","COMP-f01e7a521b5470f4"]});
